{
	"version": 1,

	"_comment": "Buffs and debuffs (status effects). Durations are simulation ticks (60 per second). A move gives them out through its 'effects' list (see combat.json / weapons.json): {id, target: enemy|self, chance 0-100, on: hit|cast, duration (optional override)}. 'stats' change a fighter's stats while the effect lasts: add = a flat amount, mul = a fraction (0.3 = +30%, -0.4 = -40%), both multiplied by the number of stacks; HEALING is a pseudo-stat that scales every kind of healing (HPREGEN and heal_percent). dot_power = damage per second as a fraction of the SOURCE's ATK, ignoring DEF (per stack). heal_percent = percent of max HP healed per second. control: stun = cannot act at all, sleep = cannot act and wakes when hurt, shock = cannot move, jump, run or dodge (can still attack and guard). A debuff's chance is moved by the source's EFFECT_ACC minus the target's EFFECT_RES. After a control effect ends the target is immune to new ones for control_immunity_ticks, so nobody can be chain-locked. Numbers are placeholders to tune by feel.",

	"_race_ultimates": "valor, unbowed, recital: statuses of the race ultimates (design/gdd/races-and-classes.md 3.7, 3.10.1). SKILL_DMG is a pseudo-stat read by the race skill_mod hook (logic/race_passives.gd skill_dmg).",

